# ## 8. Pattern note across 8 passes
#
# Each pass found a different class of issues:
# - 7-slice: structural redesign
# - fresh-eyes: heuristic dead code
# - post-rename: prefix alignment
# - 5th: build correctness (broken refs, compat stubs)
# - 6th: cross-check drift (dead files, unused imports, prefix mismatches)
# - 7th: structural consolidation (file merges)
# - 8th (this pass): line-by-line code quality
#
# The 8th pass is the first to do TRUE line-by-line review rather than
# structural patterns. The pattern that emerged: each pass revealed
# issues that were INVISIBLE to the prior passes because they were
# normalized. The user's "first principles" directive was the key:
# read each function line by line and ask "is this the cleanest
# possible implementation?"
